  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through Wednesday)\nIssued at 1242 AM CDT Thu Jul 2 2026\n\nBy Friday, a sprawling ridge will cover areas from the desert \nsouthwest to the Carolinas. This will keep highs in the upper 90s \nto around 100 degrees through Sunday. By Sunday afternoon, models \nshow a relative weakness developing in this upper level ridge over\nthe southern plains and Texas. With this weakness hanging around \nthe area through much of the first half of next week, west-central\nTexas will have a low to medium (20%-30%) chance for scattered \nshowers and thunderstorms across the entire area. Even with the \nslightly lower heights in our area, we will still have highs in \nthe mid to upper 90s.",
